        <p>
            Aerosol actuators are one of the most underestimated components in an aerosol system, yet they play a
            decisive role in how a product performs in real-world use. While cans, valves, propellants, and formulations
            receive significant attention, the actuator is the final interface between the internal aerosol system and
            the user. Its design directly controls spray pattern, discharge rate, droplet size, and directional
            accuracy.
        </p>

        <p>
            From industrial spray paints and automotive cleaners to pharmaceuticals and personal care aerosols, actuator
            engineering determines whether a product feels precise, wasteful, safe, or unreliable. This article provides
            a technically accurate explanation of aerosol actuators, focusing on their design, working principles, spray
            behavior, and industrial relevance.
        </p>

        <figure style="margin:24px 0;text-align:center;max-width:450px;">
            
            <figcaption style="font-size:0.9rem;color:#555;margin-top:8px;">Figure 1: Cross-sectional diagram of an
